  "description": "2 simple handrails for disabled and elderly resident. Minimum possible. Only attached to ground. Only on steps. Removable and reversible. Black wrought iron to fit with Regency style. Been emailing Lucy Haile. It was agreed to go ahead as a matter of urgency because elderly resident had several serious falls on steps as there is no handrail whatsoever. The lady was distressed and a prisoner in her own home. The rails installed have given her back her life and she is so relieved. I will put down that work has been completed without prior consent but effectively we have consent under the legislation to go ahead to help the resident as an emergency then apply for listed building consent after",
